    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/P_37_Ans_correct_Dhiraj.jpg\" style=\"width: 163px; height: 170px;\" /><br /><br />Two long currents carrying thin wires, both with current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>, are held by insulating threads of length L and are in equilibrium as shown in the figure, with threads making an angle &#39; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> &#39; with the vertical. If wires have a mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></math> per unit length then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is:<br />(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo></math> gravitational acceleration)",
    "image": null
  },
